        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "What is Negotiation — Money's Biggest Skill (Part 2)",
        "content": "### Types of Negotiation — 5 Approaches You Should Know\n\nAccording to the Thomas-Kilmann Conflict Mode Instrument, there are 5 negotiation styles:\n\n| Type | Description | When to Use | Indian Example |\n|------|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| **Competitive** | \"My benefit first\" — I win, you lose | Quick decisions, small stakes, when you have power | Negotiating auto-rickshaw fare — fixed rate only |\n| **Collaborative** | \"Both will win\" — Find win-win solution | Important relationships, long-term partnerships | Deciding profit-sharing in a business partnership |\n| **Compromising** | \"Let both get something\" — Middle path | When time pressure exists, both equally powerful | Roommate splitting room rent — 60-40 instead of 50-50 |\n| **Avoiding** | \"Not now\" — Avoid conflict | Trivial issues, when emotions are high | Not asking boss for salary raise right now — wrong timing |\n| **Accommodating** | \"Your point wins\" — I yield to you | When relationship matters more than money | Paying the dinner bill with a friend — relationship > ₹500 |\n\n**Pro Tip:** In most situations, the **Collaborative** approach works best. Use the Competitive approach only when stakes are low or you have clearly more power (like comparing car prices from multiple dealers).\n\n### Win-Win vs Win-Lose Mindset\n\n**Win-Lose Mindset (Competitive):**\n- \"I will save more even if it costs you\"\n- \"I will negotiate ₹100 less\"\n- Short-term benefit, long-term relationship damage\n\n**Win-Win Mindset (Collaborative):**\n- \"What solution works for both of us\"\n- \"I save ₹100 and the seller still makes a deal\"\n- Long-term relationship, repeat business, trust\n\n### How Much Money Can You Save Through Negotiation — Statistics\n\n| Negotiation Area | Average Savings | Annual Impact | Lifetime Impact (30 years) |\n|------------------|----------------|---------------|----------------------------|\n| Salary (first job) | ₹1-2 LPA more | ₹1-2 lakh/year | ₹60-120 lakh |\n| Rent | ₹2,000-5,000/month | ₹24,000-60,000/year | ₹7-18 lakh |\n| Loan rate (0.25% less) | ₹12,500/year (on ₹50L loan) | ₹12,500/year | ₹3.75 lakh |\n| Car purchase | ₹10,000-30,000 | One-time | ₹10,000-30,000 |\n| Insurance premium | ₹3,000-8,000/year | ₹3,000-8,000/year | ₹90,000-2.4 lakh |\n| Bills (monthly) | ₹500-1,500/month | ₹6,000-18,000/year | ₹1.8-5.4 lakh |\n| **Total Potential** | — | — | **₹75-150 lakh+** |\n\n---",
        "color": "#10B981",
        "emoji": "🤝",
