        "title": "Salary Negotiation — First Job's Biggest Decision (Part 3)",
        "content": "### What to Negotiate Beyond Salary\n\n| Benefit | Typical Value | Negotiable? | How to Ask |\n|---------|--------------|-------------|------------|\n| **Joining Bonus** | ₹20,000-1,00,000 | Yes | \"Could there be a joining bonus?\" |\n| **Relocation Allowance** | ₹10,000-50,000 | Yes | \"I am relocating. Is relocation support available?\" |\n| **Work From Home** | ₹2,000-5,000/month saved | Yes | \"Would 2-3 days WFH be possible?\" |\n| **Learning Budget** | ₹10,000-50,000/year | Yes | \"Is there a learning/training budget?\" |\n| **Flexible Hours** | Quality of life | Yes | \"Could I have flexible timing?\" |\n| **Extra Leave** | 2-5 days/year | Yes | \"Could I get additional leave days?\" |\n| **Performance Bonus** | 5-15% of CTC | Yes | \"Could we structure a performance bonus?\" |\n| **Stock Options (ESOP)** | Valuable | Yes (startups) | \"What is the ESOP policy?\" |\n| **Health Insurance** | ₹5-10 lakh cover | Yes | \"Is family health insurance included?\" |\n\n### Common Mistakes in Salary Negotiation\n\n| Mistake | Why It Is Bad | What to Do Instead |\n|---------|-------------|-------------------|\n| \"Whatever offer is, that is fine\" | Leaving money on the table | Always ask — worst case is they say \"no\" |\n| Not researching market rate | Negotiating blindly | Research first |\n| Accepting immediately | Looks desperate | \"I would like 24-48 hours to review\" |\n| Making it personal | \"I want more\" vs data | Use data-based arguments |\n| Not having BATNA | Hard to negotiate | Keep multiple offers ready |\n| Not getting offer in writing | Verbal promise != commitment | Get written offer letter |\n| Negotiating over email when call is better | Tone gets lost | Use phone/video call to negotiate |\n| Revealing your number first | Your expectation might be low | Let them make the first offer |\n\n---",
