        "title": "Salary Raise And Promotion — Value Increase, Money Increase",
        "content": "### When to Ask for a Raise\n\n**Best Times to Ask:**\n\n| Timing | Why It Works |\n|--------|-------------|\n| After completing major project | Proof of value |\n| Performance review cycle | Company already expects discussions |\n| After taking on new responsibilities | Your contribution has grown |\n| When market rate has increased | Market data supports you |\n| After getting a certification | Skills have improved |\n| When company is doing well | Budget is available |\n| After receiving external offer | Maximum leverage |\n\n**Worst Times to Ask:**\n\n| Timing | Why It Is Bad |\n|--------|-------------|\n| Company is downsizing | Budget cuts |\n| You just joined (within 6 months) | No proof yet |\n| Manager is in bad mood/stress | Wrong timing |\n| Right after a mistake | Track record is weak |\n\n### How to Prepare Your Case\n\n**Your Raise Preparation Checklist:**\n\n| Data Point | What to Collect | How It Helps |\n|-----------|----------------|--------------|\n| Achievements list | Specific projects, results, metrics | Shows your value |\n| Market salary data | Glassdoor, LinkedIn, AmbitionBox | Justifies the number |\n| Extra responsibilities | Tasks beyond job description | Shows growth |\n| Peer comparison | What similar roles pay | Competitive data |\n| Company performance | Revenue growth, team expansion | Shows budget availability |\n| Manager feedback | Positive emails, reviews | Proof of performance |\n| Certifications/skills | New skills learned | Shows investment in growth |\n\n### Raise Negotiation Scripts\n\n#### Script 1: Annual Review Meeting\n\n**Manager:** \"Your review is positive. We are offering you a 10% raise, bringing your salary to ₹6.6 LPA.\"\n\n---",
