        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Salary Raise And Promotion — Value Increase, Money Increase (Part 2)",
        "content": "**You:** \"Thank you, sir. I appreciate the positive review. I have prepared some data. Over the past year, I have led the [project] which saved ₹8 lakh annually, mentored 3 junior team members, and received client appreciation. Based on market rates (₹8-10 LPA for my experience), I would like to discuss a 25-30% raise. I am targeting ₹8 LPA.\"\n\n**Manager:** \"25% is too high. The budget allows 12-15%.\"\n\n**You:** \"Could we do 20% now with a 6-month review for additional raise if I hit specific targets?\"\n\n#### Script 2: After Completing Major Project\n\n**You:** \"Sir, the [project] was successfully delivered. Client gave us 9/10 satisfaction score, completed 3 weeks ahead of schedule. This project was worth ₹50 lakh. Given this contribution, I would like to discuss my compensation. Currently at ₹6 LPA, I believe ₹8 LPA reflects my value.\"\n\n### How Much Raise to Ask For\n\n| Experience Level | Typical Annual Raise | Good Raise | Ask For |\n|-----------------|---------------------|------------|---------|\n| Fresher (0-1 year) | 8-12% | 15-20% | 20-25% |\n| Junior (1-3 years) | 10-15% | 15-25% | 25-30% |\n| Mid-level (3-5 years) | 12-18% | 20-30% | 30-35% |\n| Senior (5+ years) | 15-20% | 25-40% | 35-40% |\n\n**Rule of Thumb:** Always ask 5-10% more than what you would be happy with. They will negotiate down.\n\n### What If They Say No — Alternative Asks\n\n| If They Say | Alternative Ask |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| \"Budget allows only 10%\" | \"Can we do 10% now + guaranteed review at 6 months?\" |\n| \"No raise this year\" | \"Can I get a one-time performance bonus instead?\" |\n| \"Cannot change base salary\" | \"Can we increase the variable/bonus component?\" |\n| \"No budget at all\" | \"Can I get extra leave, WFH, or learning budget?\" |\n| \"Wait for next review\" | \"Can we put this in writing with a specific date?\" |\n\n### Real Example: Amit Negotiated 40% Raise After 2 Years\n\n---",
