        "title": "Salary Raise And Promotion — Value Increase, Money Increase (Part 3)",
        "content": "**Background:** Amit, Software Developer at mid-size IT company in Pune. Joined at ₹4.5 LPA. After 2 years, current salary ₹5.4 LPA.\n\n**Amit's Preparation (3 months before review):**\n- Documented all achievements\n- Collected market data: ₹7-10 LPA for 2-year experience\n- Got 2 client appreciation emails printed\n- Listed 5 extra responsibilities\n- Practiced negotiation with a friend\n\n**The Conversation:**\n\n**Amit:** \"Sir, I have had a great 2 years. Highlights:\n1. Led project X — ₹45 lakh revenue, delivered 2 weeks early\n2. Reduced API response time by 40%\n3. Mentored 4 junior developers — 3 got promoted\n4. Completed AWS certification\n5. Client satisfaction score: 9.2/10\n\nBased on this and market research (₹7-10 LPA), I would like to discuss my compensation. I am currently at ₹5.4 LPA, and I believe ₹8 LPA reflects my value.\"\n\n**Manager:** \"You have done well. But 48% raise is not possible. Budget allows 15-20%.\"\n\n**Amit:** \"Could we do 30% now with a 6-month review? I am ready to take on the tech lead role. Alternatively, ₹7 LPA now with Senior Developer title at 12 months?\"\n\n**Manager:** \"We can offer ₹7 LPA now with Senior Developer title at 12 months.\"\n\n**Result:** ₹5.4 LPA → ₹7 LPA (30% raise) + Senior Developer title + ₹25,000 certification bonus. Over 5 years: ₹8-10 lakh more in total earnings.\n\n---",
