        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Joint Financial Planning for Couples",
        "content": "### Setting Shared Financial Goals\n\n| Timeframe | Goal Type | Examples | Timeline |\n|-----------|----------|---------|----------|\n| Short-term | Lifestyle goals | Vacation, gadgets | 0-1 year |\n| Medium-term | Asset goals | Car, home down payment | 1-5 years |\n| Long-term | Security goals | House, retirement | 5-30 years |\n\n### How to Create a Joint Budget\n\n**Combined Monthly Income: ₹98,000**\n\n| Category | Amount (₹) | % of Income |\n|----------|-----------|-------------|\n| Housing | 15,000 | 15% |\n| Groceries | 8,000 | 8% |\n| Utilities | 4,000 | 4% |\n| Transport | 5,000 | 5% |\n| Dining Out | 6,000 | 6% |\n| Entertainment | 4,000 | 4% |\n| Personal (each) | 8,000 x 2 | 16% |\n| Family Contribution | 13,000 | 13% |\n| Emergency Fund | 5,000 | 5% |\n| Car Fund | 8,000 | 8% |\n| House Fund | 10,000 | 10% |\n| SIP/Investment | 10,000 | 10% |\n| Insurance | 2,000 | 2% |\n| Buffer | 5,000 | 5% |\n| **Total** | **₹98,000** | **100%** |\n\n---",
