        "content": "### Scenario 8: Saying No to Friend's Expensive Plan\n\n**Situation:** Friends plan expensive trip (₹25,000). Budget is tight.\n\n**Script:**\n> \"Friend, the trip looks great but ₹25,000 is outside my budget. If we plan for ₹15,000 — budget hotel, local travel — I can join. Or I will plan a separate budget trip and you all can go.\"\n\n**Expected Response:** \"Let us try to plan for ₹15,000.\"\n\n**Win-Win:** Trip happens within everyone's budget.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 9: Insurance Premium Negotiation\n\n**Situation:** Health insurance ₹18,000/year. Competitor offers ₹14,000.\n\n**Script:**\n> \"I have been your customer for 2 years with no claims. [Competitor] offers ₹14,000. Can you match that? I am also willing to increase my deductible.\"\n\n**Expected Response:** \"₹15,000 with no-claim bonus.\"\n\n**Counter:** \"What if I increase deductible from ₹5,000 to ₹10,000?\"\n\n**Win-Win:** ₹13,500 premium with ₹10,000 deductible.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 10: Car/Bike Purchase Negotiation\n\n**Situation:** Bike on-road price ₹94,000. Multiple dealers offering ₹88,000-92,000.\n\n**Script:**\n> \"I have checked with other dealers — ₹88,000 on-road. If you can do ₹87,000 with free helmet and first service, I will book today with cash payment.\"\n\n**Expected Response:** \"₹88,000 with helmet.\"\n\n**Counter:** \"₹87,500 with helmet and free first service. Final offer.\"\n\n**Win-Win:** ₹87,500 deal, dealer gets cash sale today.\n\n---",
