        "content": "### Top 10 Negotiation Rules\n\n| # | Rule | Why It Matters |\n|---|------|----------------|\n| 1 | Always research first | Knowledge is power |\n| 2 | Let them speak first | They might reveal their position |\n| 3 | Use silence strategically | Pause creates pressure |\n| 4 | Focus on value, not price | Justify your worth |\n| 5 | Have a BATNA | Know your alternatives |\n| 6 | Be willing to walk away | Strongest negotiating position |\n| 7 | Get everything in writing | Verbal promises are not binding |\n| 8 | Stay calm and respectful | Emotions weaken your position |\n| 9 | Find win-win solutions | Build long-term relationships |\n| 10 | Practice regularly | Negotiation is a skill |\n\n### Money Rules for Couples\n\n| # | Rule | Implementation |\n|---|------|---------------|\n| 1 | No secrets about money | Full financial disclosure |\n| 2 | Budget together | Monthly money meeting |\n| 3 | Respect different styles | Saver + Spender = balance |\n| 4 | Set shared goals | Short, medium, long-term |\n| 5 | Keep some independence | Individual spending allowance |\n| 6 | Plan for emergencies | 6-month emergency fund |\n| 7 | Review and adjust | Quarterly plan review |\n\n### Final Quick Tips\n\n- **Start small** — Negotiate auto fare, grocery price, internet bill\n- **Be confident** — You deserve fair deals\n- **Use data** — Market rates are your weapon\n- **Practice** — Every negotiation makes you better\n- **Celebrate** — Every ₹1 saved is ₹1 earned\n- **Communicate** — Money talks prevent money fights\n- **Plan together** — Shared goals build stronger relationships\n\n---",
